WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:02.980
Have you ever heard about Zhong Shanshan?

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:07.919
At the end of 2020, Zhong Shanshan actually
became the richest person in Asia with a net

00:00:07.919 --> 00:00:11.250
worth of $77.8 billion.

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:16.230
His net worth didn’t just stop there either,
in January of 2021, Shanshan would reach a

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:19.250
peak net worth of $95 billion.

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:24.120
Since then, his net worth has cooled off quite
substantially as he now sits at the high $60

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.330
billion mark.

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:30.100
But given that he was at just $2 billion a
year ago, I don’t think he’s complaining.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:34.330
The first assumption I had when I read about
this was that Shanshan likely founded China’s

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:36.550
next tech or manufacturing giant.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:41.290
But, in reality, Shanshan’s wealth doesn’t
come from selling high margin software or

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:43.010
high volume consumer goods.

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:47.640
No, Shanshan actually made his fortune selling
bottled water.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:50.250
Wait a minute, this makes no sense.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:55.070
A bottled water company founder is wealthier
than the founders of Alibaba, Tencent, and

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:58.310
Foxconn and he made most of his wealth in
a single year?

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:01.680
Clearly, there’s more going on here than
what meets the eye.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:07.190
So, here’s the story of how Zhong Shanshan
really became Asia’s richest person by just

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:10.010
selling water.

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:13.880
Before we get into Shanshan’s story, let's
first lay out some context as to how absurd

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:15.380
this achievement is.

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:20.670
The beverage industry is basically impossible
to break into due to insanely low profit margins

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:23.409
and how much of a stronghold the market leaders
have.

00:01:23.409 --> 00:01:28.150
Just take a look at the most popular bottled
water companies such as aquafina, Dasani,

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:30.450
Nestle waters, and smart water.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:34.760
Aside from Nestle waters which is obviously
made by Nestle, the other brands don’t seem

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.260
to be associated with large conglomerates.

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:41.190
Though their name doesn’t suggest such a
relationship, Aquafina is actually owned by

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:46.350
Pepsi, dasani is owned by coca cola, and smart
water is owned by energy brands which is owned

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:47.600
by coca cola.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:52.100
Pepsi and Coca Cola basically own the beverage
industry mainly because they were the first

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:56.979
people there, so it’s no wonder why Kevin
O’leary obliterates every beverage company

00:01:56.979 --> 00:01:59.570
that makes its way onto shark tank.

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:04.040
With all of that being said, let’s take
a look at how Shanshan defied the odds.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:07.500
Starting off, Shanshan was born in Hangzhou
China in 1954.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:12.409
We’ve heard of top billionaires dropping
out of college and sometimes even high school,

00:02:12.409 --> 00:02:16.400
but Shanshan actually dropped out of elementary
school at the age of 12.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:19.790
Unlike other billionaires though, he didn’t
drop out to start his own business.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:23.409
He was actually forced to drop out because
of the cultural revolution.

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:28.180
The cultural revolution was a massive communist
led uprising within China designed to purge

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:30.239
the country of capitalists.

00:02:30.239 --> 00:02:34.349
During the revolution, all economic activity
was halted and hundreds of thousands of people

00:02:34.349 --> 00:02:35.529
would die.

00:02:35.529 --> 00:02:40.469
Shanshan’s parents would be one of the people
that were persecuted by the authorities.

00:02:40.469 --> 00:02:45.379
So, education was one of the last things on
Shanshan’s mind and he would find a rather

00:02:45.379 --> 00:02:48.890
uncontroversial job in construction throughout
his teenage years.

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:53.249
Right after the cultural revolution ended
in 1976 though, Shanshan would be quick to

00:02:53.249 --> 00:02:58.219
go to college at the Zhejiang Radio &amp; TV University
where he studied Chinese.

00:02:58.219 --> 00:03:03.779
This degree led him to picking up a job as
a journalist at Zhejiang Daily up until 1988.

00:03:03.779 --> 00:03:07.629
Till this point, Shanshan had mainly just
worked on getting by and making sure he had

00:03:07.629 --> 00:03:08.909
food on the table.

00:03:08.909 --> 00:03:13.359
However, as economic restrictions became looser
in the late 1980s, Shanshan would start his

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.769
first business in 1988.

00:03:15.769 --> 00:03:20.400
This business was a very simple grocery business
that Shanshan ran at a tourist island named

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.400
Hainan.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:26.029
He ended up selling mushrooms, prawns, and
turtles to tourists and locals, but this effort

00:03:26.029 --> 00:03:27.569
didn’t last too long.

00:03:27.569 --> 00:03:31.799
We aren’t exactly sure why he gave up this
local business, but Shanshan would end up

00:03:31.799 --> 00:03:33.419
getting another job.

00:03:33.419 --> 00:03:37.159
This time, he worked as a sales agent at the
Wahaha beverage company.

00:03:37.159 --> 00:03:40.589
And this is where he would get the idea to
start his own beverage company.

00:03:40.589 --> 00:03:46.750
You see, bottled water was and still is extremely
popular within China and for good reason.

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:51.669
Unlike the US where I still have no clue as
to why people buy bottled water, in China,

00:03:51.669 --> 00:03:55.529
natural water sources are oftentimes heavily
polluted due to the significant amounts of

00:03:55.529 --> 00:03:56.859
manufacturing activity.

00:03:56.859 --> 00:04:01.549
Also, the sewage and water treatment facilities
in China are quite terrible.

00:04:01.549 --> 00:04:06.150
Not to mention, many of the water pipes in
China were installed before 1968, and the

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:08.749
pipes have significantly rusted since then.

00:04:08.749 --> 00:04:13.359
So, drinking tap water in China is a serious
health risk as it often contains large amounts

00:04:13.359 --> 00:04:19.750
of bacteria, viruses, chlorine, lead, mercury,
aluminum, and who knows what else.

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:23.630
Given the undrinkable nature of tap water,
basically all of China had resorted to buying

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:27.420
bottled water and more specifically distilled
bottled water.

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:32.480
Now, distilled water is perfectly safe to
drink, but it does lack the dissolved minerals

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:34.530
that regular clean drinking water has.

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:39.260
This includes minerals like calcium and magnesium
which are actually beneficial for health.

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:44.000
In the 1990s, China had plenty of distilled
water brands, but it seemed like no one was

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:47.040
offering simple clean drinking water with
minerals.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:49.610
And this is precisely what Shanshan would
target.

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:54.720
In 1996, Shanshan would found a bottled water
company which would eventually become Nongfu

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:55.720
Spring.

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:59.410
Their primary marketing pitch was that unlike
the rest of the industry, they didn’t remove

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:01.500
natural minerals from their water.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.480
Given that the Chinese people were already
a bit worried about just drinking distilled

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:08.490
water with no minerals, Nongfu springs took
off.

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:12.450
After this major success, Nongfu springs would
go ahead and launch a variety of fruit drinks

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:14.010
in 2003.

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:18.380
Nongfu springs did specifically target teenagers
with these fruit drinks and they did try to

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.590
craft some unique marketing material.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:25.070
But by this point, the brand image is what
was really propelling Nongfu forward.

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:28.930
Within China, Nongfu springs became known
as the up and coming beverage company that

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:31.590
was more natural and healthier than rest.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:36.100
And this perception allowed them to roll out
a handful of new products over the next decade

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:42.350
including vitamin water in 2010, sugar free
tea in 2011, milk tea in 2012, orange and

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:46.830
apple juice in 2016, and most recently coffee
in 2019.

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:50.600
In the meantime, they have also expanded their
water production to pull water from 10 different

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:54.440
natural sources throughout china and even
one in new Zealand.

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:58.491
Aside from expanding their product lineup,
Shanshan has placed significant emphasis on

00:05:58.491 --> 00:06:00.390
marketing to grow the business.

00:06:00.390 --> 00:06:04.910
One notable instance of clever product placement
was during the 2016 G20 leader’s summit.

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:10.810
Shanshan was able to get Nongfu water into
the event and presidents Xi, Obama, Putin,

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:16.510
Trudeau and many others would end up sipping
the mineral rich water throughout the event.

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:20.890
Similarly, in 2017, Nongfu would spend $18
million to become the title sponsor of the

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:23.140
first season of Rap of China.

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:26.160
This was of course an effort to appeal to
China’s youth.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:30.340
Anyway, through such clever marketing moves
and positioning in the marketplace, Shanshan

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:34.730
was successfully able to break into the bottled
water industry and grow Nongfu springs into

00:06:34.730 --> 00:06:39.710
a multi billion dollar business while growing
his personal wealth to $2 billion by 2020.

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:43.430
So, that's the more natural part of Shanshan’s
business success.

00:06:43.430 --> 00:06:47.670
Of course, he always had the blessings of
the CCP as you can’t achieve any sort of

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.100
business success in China without that.

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:54.830
But, in 2020, Shanshan would transition from
just being on the good side of the CCP to

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:56.760
being their star child.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:07:01.560
Over the years, the CCP has had a very complicated
relationship with billionaires and business

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:03.900
tycoons within the country.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:08.900
As the name of the party suggests, they are
communist and believe in communist ideologies.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:12.830
This includes the idea that all property is
publicly owned and that each person works

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:15.170
and is paid according to their abilities and
needs.

00:07:15.170 --> 00:07:19.980
Ideally, there would be no billionaires or
business moguls in such a system, and that’s

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:22.670
how it was in the 1950s and 1960s.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:27.680
But, since the death of Mao Zedong, the CCP
has gotten looser and looser when it comes

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:29.170
to the economy.

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:34.270
You see, the CCP realized in the 1970s and
80s that they couldn’t continue to limit

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:37.290
economic freedom if they wanted to grow into
a world power.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:42.010
So, they started letting people open businesses
which grew China's economic output and allowed

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:43.840
them to compete on a world stage.

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:47.730
Don’t let this freedom fool you though,
billionaires in China are handpicked by the

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:52.290
CCP and closely monitored to ensure that these
billionaires don’t step out of line.

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:57.080
If they do step out of line and oppose the
CCP or try to flee the country, the CCP will

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:59.430
be sure to take appropriate action.

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:03.610
Many people like to speculate that nefarious
things happen to these billionaires, but we’re

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:06.000
not going to go down that road in this video.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:09.410
If you guys are interested in this topic,
then be sure to check out Jake Tran’s video

00:08:09.410 --> 00:08:10.660
on the subject.

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:14.970
What we can confirm though is that the businesses
of such billionaires will be punished with

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:17.510
restrictive regulation and litigation.

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:21.560
Meanwhile, billionaires who are on the good
side of the CCP will be blessed with loose

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:23.900
regulation and aid from the government.

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:28.740
And it seems like Zhong Shanshan just replaced
Jack Ma as the star child of the CCP.

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:33.399
If you guys didn’t know, Jack Ma founded
Alibaba and used to be China’s richest man.

00:08:33.399 --> 00:08:38.959
However, in late October he would make some
remarks that the CCP weren’t big fans of.

00:08:38.959 --> 00:08:43.120
And after this, he would go missing for 3
months before making a low key return and

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:45.019
laying low ever since.

00:08:45.019 --> 00:08:49.310
A striking difference between Jack Ma and
Zhong Shanshan is their personalities.

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:54.829
Jack Ma is extremely charismatic and outspoken
while Shanshan is extremely reserved and quiet.

00:08:54.829 --> 00:08:59.300
Maybe the CCP realized that they shouldn’t
bet on outspoken individuals like Jack Ma

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:02.309
when it comes to representing the elite class
of China.

00:09:02.309 --> 00:09:04.839
And this is where things get interesting.

00:09:04.839 --> 00:09:09.600
After Jack Ma’s comments, on November 13,
2020, president Xi would go ahead and personally

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:14.660
stop the IPO of ant group which is another
company founded by Jack Ma.

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:20.029
On this exact same day, Nongfu stock would
start to pump after two months of stagnation.

00:09:20.029 --> 00:09:23.830
Within the next two trading days, Nongfu stock
would rally 20%.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:27.470
But here’s the thing, there was no news
from Nongfu.

00:09:27.470 --> 00:09:31.720
No press releases, no new products, no earnings
reports, nothing.

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:36.649
And guess what, this pump was exactly enough
to get Zhong Shanshan to overtake Jack Ma

00:09:36.649 --> 00:09:40.480
as China’s richest man on November 17, 2020.

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:43.720
After this random pump though, the stock would
go back into stagnation mode for the next

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:44.720
month.

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:49.170
Between December 15 and January 8 though,
Nongfu Spring stock would roar upwards once

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:52.940
again growing a massive 50% within weeks.

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:58.230
But once again, there was no major news coming
out from Nongfu during this time period either.

00:09:58.230 --> 00:10:01.819
There was, however, massive news coming out
about Jack Ma though.

00:10:01.819 --> 00:10:06.110
Between December 13 and December 31, every
news organization was busy covering how Jack

00:10:06.110 --> 00:10:10.170
Ma had lost billions and how he didn’t even
attend his own talent show.

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:14.839
We saw headlines like How China Lost Patience
with Jack Ma, Its Loudest Billionaire.

00:10:14.839 --> 00:10:19.550
Jack Ma's wealth tumbles by $12 billion in
2 months as China seeks to shrink the billionaire's

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:20.869
financial empire.

00:10:20.869 --> 00:10:24.760
Jack Ma disappears from his own talent show
and so on and so forth.

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:29.100
At the exact same time, we also saw articles
describing how Zhong Shanshan just became

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:31.139
the richest person in Asia.

00:10:31.139 --> 00:10:35.579
It almost seems like wealth was being transferred
from Jack Ma to Zhong and that Zhong’s rise

00:10:35.579 --> 00:10:39.579
to the top was being used to reduce news coverage
surrounding Jack ma’s disappearance.

00:10:39.579 --> 00:10:41.380
It doesn't just stop right there either.

00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:46.819
At the end of January, Jack Ma would make
a return, and suddenly all of Zhong’s new

00:10:46.819 --> 00:10:51.449
found wealth would disappear shortly after
as Nongfu stock crashed from $65 a share back

00:10:51.449 --> 00:10:56.130
down to $40 a share, exactly where it was
in September and october.

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:59.690
And during this entire time period, there
were no negative news pieces coming out about

00:10:59.690 --> 00:11:00.690
Nongfu.

00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:04.749
I mean if you just take a look at the stock
graph, it seems like a pump and dump.

00:11:04.749 --> 00:11:09.860
And just keep in mind, this is not a company
like Tesla or Apple that is fueled by hype.

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:12.860
This is a water bottle company.

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:16.980
This isn’t to say that Nongfu is not a legitimate
company or that Zhong didn’t work extremely

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:20.610
hard to build Nongfu into a multi billion
dollar conglomerate.

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:25.230
But more recently, it does seem like there's
more happening than what meets the eye.

00:11:25.230 --> 00:11:27.709
What do you guys think about Zhong’s journey
to the top?

00:11:27.709 --> 00:11:28.790
Comment that down below.

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:32.899
Also, drop a like if you guys found this analysis
rather intriguing.

